The Python core, synthetic acceptance tests and standalone documentation were
newly authored for this candidate with AI assistance. Concepts were assessed
from a private bounded-context helper; private source/history/configuration was
not imported. The required-check workflow derives from an owner-controlled
repository template, with strict success and same-run SHA selection.

CPython and its embedded SQLite are prerequisites supplied separately by the
consumer and are not redistributed in this wheel. Development-only tools and
external workflow actions retain their upstream licenses and are not pip runtime
requirements or bundled wheel implementation code.
